        (v_dataset_id, ores_utility_system_tenant_id_fn(), 'aefbe509-ce57-52dc-9e67-473f810b9e97', 0, 'FXVolatilities', 'FXVolatility', 'Conventions', 'curveconfig.xsd', '/CurveConfiguration/FXVolatilities/FXVolatility/Conventions', 10, 'string', false, 'Conventions', 'FX conventions object ID that is used to determine the at-the-money type and delta type of the volatility quotes, these default to AtmDeltaNeutral and Spot for option tenors <= 2Y and AtmDeltaNeutral and Fwd for option tenors > 2Y if the conventions ID is omitted or left blank.', 'FX conventions object ID that is used to determine the at-the-money type and delta type of the volatility quotes, these default to AtmDeltaNeutral and Spot for option tenors <= 2Y and AtmDeltaNeutral and Fwd for option tenors > 2Y if the conventions ID is omitted or left blank. Furthermore, the conventions hold information on the side of risk reversals (RiskReversalInFavorOf, defaults to Call) and the quote style of butterflies (ButterflyStyle, defaults to Broker), these latter two are relevant for BF, RR market data input. See for more details.', 'AtmDeltaNeutral and Spot for option tenors <= 2Y and AtmDeltaNeutral and Fwd for option tenors > 2Y if the conventions ID is omitted or left blank.', 'Text.', '1.8.0.7 or earlier', null),
